1000 GOSUB 9525:GOSUB 6100:BM$="David had never felt so good in the morning before. Susanna wasn't there,\but her scent still lingered on the bed.":GOSUB 5100
1010 GOSUB 6110:BM$="But after taking a shower, David looked in the mirror and his mood soured\instantly.":GOSUB 5100
1020 BM$="He had another bruise on his shoulder. It was as if the events of his\nightmares also occurred in the real world.":GOSUB 5100
1040 BM$="David shook his head, as if to chase away the thought, and left the\bathroom. The late wake-up call was ringing.":GOSUB 5100
1045 GOSUB 6200:GOSUB 8030:GOSUB 9010
1050 GOSUB 5205:GOSUB 6300:GOSUB 5800:BM$="David: Hey, good morning Susanna. I slept great last night. I'm feeling\better than ever.":GOSUB 5100
1055 GOSUB 5205:GOSUB 6340:GOSUB 5800:BM$="Susanna: I'm glad to hear that.\Today you'll have your first performance in Italy. Good luck, David.":GOSUB 5100
1056 GOSUB 5205:GOSUB 6300:GOSUB 5800:BM$="David: ...Thank you, Susanna.":GOSUB 5100:GOSUB 5200
1060 COMMON FO:ISET X:BM$="After hearing Susanna's voice, David forgot all about his nightmares.":GOSUB 5100
1100 GOSUB 9535:GOSUB 6120:BM$="Once the sun had set, their first concert in Rome began.":GOSUB 5100
1120 BM$="Andrew: David, let's make it happen again tonight!":GOSUB 5100
1130 BM$="Alan: C'mon, let's go! David, take us by the storm!":GOSUB 5100
1140 BM$="As David walked under the spotlight, he was greeted by the cheers of his\fans. The moment the song's intro started playing, the crowd screamed so\loudly that the stage itself seemed to tremble.":GOSUB 5100
1150 GOSUB 9515:GOSUB 6140:BM$="The crowd's excitement would only increase as the band kept playing, to\the point where it had become next to impossible to keep them in check.":GOSUB 5100
1160 BM$="While David screamed his song, some among the audience were scratching\their faces into a bloody mess. At first it was only one, but this behavior\was seemingly spreading.":GOSUB 5100
1170 GOSUB 9505:BM$="The sound of the ambulance's sirens only added to the song's power, as\paramedics with their stretchers came and went uninterruptedly.":GOSUB 5100
1180 BM$="A police officer spoke to Susanna.":GOSUB 5100
1190 GOSUB 6130:GOSUB 1300
